#
# A mission built on the Open Universe ENGINE.
#
# `universe_core` (an OpenUniverse mastlib, listed in story.json) does the work: it
# generates systems from a seed, runs the jump drive, sides, reputation, trade and jobs.
# What THIS mission supplies is a universe to run - authored as data in `my_universe.amd`
# - and a @map to start it from.
#
# The engine carries no @map of its own, so the one below is the only entry the start
# screen shows.
#

# Which universe to load. universe_core's own universe.mast declares
# `default shared UNIVERSE_SELECT = "Default"`; a mission's story.mast compiles BEFORE the
# mastlibs, so this `default` runs first and wins.
default shared UNIVERSE_SELECT = "My Universe"

# How the crew travels. Both are set here, before the mastlibs, for the same reason as
# the line above: LegendaryMissions' Quests tab declares the first one False, and whoever
# says `default` first wins.
#   QUEST_ENGAGE_ENABLED  puts the Engage button on Helm's Quests tab. Without it the crew
#                         can take a cargo run and never fly it.
#   WAYPOINTS_ENABLED     keeps a list of the named places the crew has been, so they can
#                         Engage a way back.
default shared QUEST_ENGAGE_ENABLED = True
default shared WAYPOINTS_ENABLED = True


#
# Register the universe so the engine can find it. The engine scans for `type: universe/*`
# labels and reads the named .amd relative to THIS mission folder.
#
=== universe_my_universe
metadata:``` yaml
type: universe/my_universe
key: my_universe
display: My Universe
universe: my_universe.amd
```
    ->END


@map/my_universe "My Universe"
" Explore a procedurally generated frontier. Engage the jump drive on the Navigation
" console to travel between systems - the same seed always regenerates the same galaxy.
metadata:``` yaml
Properties:
  Main:
    Start: 'gui_drop_down("$text: {START_MODE};list: Continue, New Game", var="START_MODE")'
    Player Ships: 'gui_int_slider("$text:int;low: 1.0;high:8.0;", var= "PLAYER_COUNT")'
    Difficulty: 'gui_int_slider("$text:int;low: 1.0;high:11.0;", var= "DIFFICULTY")'
    Seed: 'gui_input("desc: Integer (0 = random);", var="seed_value")'
GameCode:
  - PLAYER_COUNT
  - DIFFICULTY
  - seed_value
```
    UNIVERSE_SELECT = "My Universe"
    # Everything from here is the engine's. `universe_map_begin` lives in universe_core.
    jump universe_map_begin
